   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# LayerStream test 2 - MiniMax H3 image-to-video, 1 MP x 15 s\n\nNeeds the custom node pack `osiworx-pack` (folder `custom_nodes/osiworx-pack`, module `layer`) and a ComfyUI that has `comfy.ldm.minimax` (MiniMax H3 support).\n\nWith default launch flags a 1 MP / 15 s clip did not fit a 24 GB card (author's 4090). **Two ways to get it to run - try both:**\n1. No node: start ComfyUI with `--vram-headroom 10 --disable-pinned-memory` (bypass the `LayerStream: H3 Chunking` node). This alone fixed it on the test machine.\n2. With the node (default in this graph): attention and MLP run in token chunks. Output is **bit-identical** to the stock model\n   (verified frame by frame) and ran under a hard 8 GB cap on PyTorch's own allocations (weights are limited separately by the flag, so\n   this does not by itself prove an 8 GB card works). About 10 % slower; smaller chunk = less VRAM, slower.\n\nAudio: H3 generates sound together with the video. The graph decodes it with the H3 audio VAE (`VAEDecodeAudio`) and muxes it into the video\n(`CreateVideo` -> audio). The audio is identical with and without the chunking node.\n\nUse ~6 steps with the turbo LoRA. 1-2 step results are degenerate by design (broken details are not a bug of the node).\nPick your own start image in `Load Image`.\n\nVideo size: the `Megapixel Size` node (osiworx-pack, module `wos`) takes the width/height from your start image for a target of 1.05 MP,\nkeeping its aspect ratio. It is set to **multiples of 32** because H3 works on 32-pixel tokens (16x VAE x 2x2 patch). A square image gives 1024x1024."
   ]
  }
 ],
